========
ASSIMULO
========

INSTALL
=======

*REQUIREMENTS
	- Python-3 (with headers)
	- Numpy, Scipy, Pylab
	- Sundials-2.5/2.6/3.1/4.1
	- Cython >= 3
    - C-compiler
    - Fortran-compiler
    - BLAS
    - LAPACK

Installation is performed using the command:

	'python setup.py install --sundials-home=/path/to/sundials --blas-home=/path/to/blas --lapack-home=/path/to/lapack'
	
Assimulo is then installed under Python dist-packages. 
To test the installation, run "pytest".

Building with meson-python (Python >= 3.12, where numpy.distutils no longer exists)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    pip install --no-build-isolation \
        -Csetup-args=-Dsundials-home=$CONDA_PREFIX \
        -Csetup-args=-Dsuperlu-home=$CONDA_PREFIX \
        -Csetup-args=-Dblas-home=$CONDA_PREFIX/lib -Csetup-args=-Dlapack-home=$CONDA_PREFIX/lib .

Options (meson.options): sundials-home, superlu-home, blas-home, lapack-home, fortran
(auto/enabled/disabled), extra-fortran-flags (default --std=legacy). Needs meson-python,
Cython >= 3, numpy, a C compiler and, for the Fortran solvers, gfortran. The build produces
the same 19 extension modules as setup.py with the same compiler flags; tools/dump_examples.py
and tests/test_build_equivalence.py compare two builds bit for bit.
